// The baseline every policy set opens with.
//
// Cedar denies by default, so without a permit nothing is ever allowed and
// a set of forbid rules would reject every request. These permits establish
// "allowed unless a policy objects"; each active policy is a forbid that
// overrides them, which is what gives an AND across policies.
//
// One permit per decision point: a permit scoped to a single action would
// leave the other denying everything. An admin's own permit cannot widen
// access — a forbid always wins.
@id("base_allow_issue")
permit (principal, action == Vouch::Action::"IssueToken", resource);

@id("base_allow_exchange")
permit (principal, action == Vouch::Action::"ExchangeToken", resource);
